# Fix blank document thumbnails by sanitizing cache directory names and adding fallback error placeholder (#675)

## Summary
1. Sanitizes user IDs used as `CacheManager` directory keys to contain only filesystem-safe characters (`[a-zA-Z0-9_-]`), preventing cache directory creation failures on modern Android / HyperOS when user IDs contain `@`, `:`, or slashes.
2. Replaces empty `SizedBox.shrink()` error widgets in `DocumentPreview` with a structured document placeholder icon and logs thumbnail loading failures via `errorListener`.

## Problem
In issue #675, thumbnails rendered as blank white boxes on devices running Android 14+ / HyperOS even though thumbnail HTTP 200 responses were received.
Because `appUserId` (often containing format `user@https://host:port`) was passed directly as the `CacheManager` configuration key, filesystem path creation failed silently on restricted environments. Furthermore, `DocumentPreview` swallowed errors with `errorWidget: (ctxt, msg, _) => SizedBox.shrink()`, showing empty boxes with no placeholder.

## Solution
- Added `HomeShellWidget.sanitizeCacheKey` to strip non-alphanumeric characters from cache directory names.
- Updated `DocumentPreview` to display a themed document icon placeholder in `errorWidget` and log decoding/network failures via `errorListener`.
- Added unit tests in `test/src/features/home/sanitize_cache_key_test.dart`.

